From 2cd2517a0a1edcee885ee5996971d54bc8356b85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 19:44:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix static initialization and theme area bounds

userland_B.ld set ALLOW_INIT_ARRAY = 1, but the production userland is
linked with rt0_no_init_array.cpp, so .init_array is never executed.
Every global initialized from a (now mutable) Palette color stayed zero:
the Python turtle object, curve color names/picker, plot pattern
transparency, sum graph legend format, Python selection highlight and
USB screen colors. Restore the linker guard and make these values
constant-initialized or computed at use time.

Also bound-check every offset/size read from the Theme Area before
dereferencing it, skip the Theme Area on the simulator (fixed device
address), and restore shared/ion/src/shared/dummy/init.cpp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01S8rZuXVCv5NTE5FNLjFwki
